<% content_for :title, "Devices — Tinkerex" %>
<%= render "settings/crumbs", current: "Devices" %>

<%# YOUR DESKTOP DEVICES (Settings::DevicesController). No accent on this page: there is no one
    action it exists for, and signing out is a danger link on each row (design-system.md rule 13).

    WHAT IT IS FOR FIRST, THEN ONE HONEST NOTE (UX audit F6). On a sync-server library a device holds a
    second key, on the sync server, that signing out here does not end (CLAUDE.md §14j's deliberate
    split), so the note says that in the same breath as what signing out does, and names the next
    step for a lost device. Elsewhere there is no second key, and the page never mentions one. %>
<div class="page-head">
  <h1>Devices</h1>
</div>

<p class="muted">
  The desktop apps and assistants connected to your account, most recently used first. Sign one
  out when you stop using it, or as soon as it is lost.
</p>
<p class="muted">
  Signing a device out ends its access to this server, and it needs your password to sign in again.
  <% if capabilities.syncable? %>
    It can still sync files until it is removed from the sync server too, which this page cannot do
    yet: for a lost device, ask whoever runs this server to remove it there.
  <% end %>
  Changing your password signs out every device.
  <% if @idle_limit %>
    A device unused for <%= pluralize(@idle_limit.in_days.round, "day") %> is signed out on its own.
  <% end %>
</p>

<ul class="settings-list">
  <% @devices.each do |device| %>
    <%= render "settings/devices/device", device: device, idle_limit: @idle_limit,
                                          url: settings_device_path(device), owner: nil %>
  <% end %>
  <% if @devices.empty? %>
    <li class="empty inline">Nothing is connected to this account.</li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<h2>Connect an AI assistant</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Claude Code, Claude Desktop or any MCP client can work in this library through a token of its
  own, made here and shown once. It appears in the list above and is signed out the same way.
</p>
<%# scope: :device -- form_with url: has no model, so scope: is what names the field device[name],
    which Settings::DevicesController#create reads (CLAUDE.md §14d). The value is stated, because a
    scoped field with no model falls back to an @device this page never sets. Turbo is off on this
    form: the answer is a page carrying a secret shown once, rendered rather than redirected to, and
    a full page load is the one shape every Turbo version renders. The submit is a quiet button:
    this page has no accent (design-system.md rule 13). size: nil is load-bearing: given maxlength
    and no size, text_field copies 80 into size, an 80-character field that pushed this page to
    scrollWidth 609 at 375px (rule 11, measured). %>
<%= form_with url: settings_devices_path, scope: :device, class: "settings-add", data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
  <label>
    <span>Name</span>
    <%= f.text_field :name, value: Settings::DevicesController::DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_NAME, required: true,
                     maxlength: 80, size: nil, autocomplete: "off" %>
  </label>
  <%= f.submit "Connect", class: "btn" %>
<% end %>
